crates/llm-provider-kit contains code and data from oh-my-pi, used under the
MIT License; see crates/llm-provider-kit/NOTICE.

crates/agent-core/src/anthropic-skills.json indexes the skills in
https://github.com/anthropics/skills (names, descriptions and license fields).
Skills are downloaded from that repository when installed and remain under
their own licenses.

crates/lynshen-sandbox/src/windows (sid.rs, token.rs, acl.rs, process.rs)
contains code adapted from OpenAI Codex (codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs),
https://github.com/openai/codex, licensed under the Apache License 2.0:

    OpenAI Codex
    Copyright 2025 OpenAI

The adapted files say so at the top and were changed for LynShen.

Android phone control (crates/agent-core/src/android.rs) downloads, when the
user installs it, android-use 1.2.0 (https://github.com/austinintelligence/android-use)
into ~/.lynshen/tools/android-use. LynShen does not bundle it; its tool
descriptions follow android-use's. android-use is used under the MIT License:

